# Line endings are pinned rather than left to each machine's git config, because this project
# asserts on them.
#
# Most expected values in the test suite are raw string literals, whose newlines are the physical
# bytes of the .cs file. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true — the default on GitHub's
# windows runners — turns those into CRLF, while the inputs beside them use "\n" escapes and so
# stay LF. The formatter preserves its input's terminator, faithfully returns LF, and 104 tests
# fail on a difference that exists only in the checkout. Normalising to LF everywhere removes the
# variable rather than teaching every assertion to ignore it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# …except the fixtures, whose exact bytes are the thing under test. Encoding and terminator
# behaviour is asserted against these files, so git must hand them over as committed and convert
# nothing — including a deliberately CRLF fixture, should one be added. .editorconfig exempts the
# same paths from editor normalisation, for the same reason.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# Binary, so git neither diffs nor converts them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.vsix binary
